### 4. Online Adaptation Decision Process (Monitoring → Analysis → Planning → Verification → Execution)

This is **the heart** of the English blueprint's process-oriented structure. The English chapter devotes §5.4 as the major section containing five subsections that trace the runtime decision process step-by-step.

| Subsection | English Blueprint | Persian Chapter 5 | Status |
|-----------|-------------------|-------------------|--------|
| **Monitoring & Feature Extraction** (§5.4.1) | ✅ Detailed: sensor data → preprocessing → feature extraction → state vector construction → validation → dissemination. Includes formal state vector contract ($s_t \in \mathbb{R}^d$) and explicit process boundary. | ⚠️ §5.4 covers data collection and state construction, but much less detail. No formal state vector *contract*, no explicit *process boundary* statement. | **Partial** |
| **Analysis & Context Interpretation** (§5.4.2) | ✅ Analyzer receives state, evaluates against goals, triggers adaptation. Explicit figure. | ⚠️ §5.5 briefly covers analysis and triggering, but no dedicated activity diagram reference. | **Partial** |
| **Planning: Adaptation Option Prediction** (§5.4.3) | ✅ Detailed: trigger → model retrieval (Stage 6) → Q-value evaluation → argmax selection. Explicit "pure inference" process boundary — no learning here. | ✅ §5.6 covers this well. Explicitly states "no learning occurs" during inference — matches blueprint. | **✅ Good** |
| **Verification** (§5.4.4) | ✅ Detailed: receives candidate option → retrieves runtime model → UPPAAL-SMC statistical model checking → extracts QoS metrics → produces dual outputs (decision feedback + learning reward). Framed as "runtime justification" with reward as *by-product*. | ⚠️ §5.7 covers verification via UPPAAL-SMC but frames it quite differently — emphasizes "if risk is too high, adaptation is blocked", treats reward generation as a primary output. Missing: (a) dual output distinction, (b) assumptions/limitations, (c) framing as "runtime justification". | **Partial — Different Framing** |
| **Execution** (§5.4.5) | ✅ Short but precise: Executor retrieves option (Stage 8) → applies to managed system (Stage 9). Explicit figure. | ✅ §5.8 covers this adequately. | **✅ Good** |
| **MAPE-K Control Loop Summary figure** | ✅ Optional validation figure (Fig. 6) | ❌ Not present | **Missing** |

> [!IMPORTANT]
> The English blueprint has **5 dedicated activity diagram figures** (monitoring, analysis, prediction, verification, execution) plus a MAPE-K summary figure. The Persian chapter has essentially **1 architecture figure** (the RS-DRL architecture from the article). This is a major gap — the process models are the entire contribution of this chapter.

